# Eluge, the Shoreless Sea: "It's an Island in addition to its other types for as long as it has a flood counter on it" ends when
# the counter is removed (CR 611.2b), and a new flood counter from Eluge's next trigger makes it an Island again by a new effect.
# Turn 3: Eluge (Black Lotus and an Island) floods Bot1's Mountain and is 2/2. Turn 4: Bot2's Vampire Hexmage (its own Black
# Lotus) is sacrificed to remove all counters from the Mountain: it is only a Mountain again and Eluge is 1/1.
# Turn 5: the first instant of the turn, Brainstorm, gets no reduction - no land Bot1 controls has a flood counter - so an Island
# pays its {U}, and no mana is left over. Eluge attacks and floods the Mountain again: an Island again, Eluge 3/3 (two Islands and
# the Mountain). The second Brainstorm is not the first instant or sorcery spell of the turn, so it costs its full {U}, which the
# Mountain pays as an Island, again with nothing left over. Bot2 takes 3.

